WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.591
Step 1. Open the observation definitions list.

1.2
00:00:03.591 --> 00:00:09.475
An observation definition is the template that staff use to record the results of

1.3
00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:15.060
one test. In Settings, under Clinical, select Observation Definitions.

2.1
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:20.476
Step 2. Start a new observation definition. Select Add Definition.

2.2
00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:24.890
Care opens the Create Observation Definition form.

3.1
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.012
Step 3. Fill in the basic information.

3.2
00:00:28.012 --> 00:00:32.924
Enter the Title, Description, Category, Data Type and LOINC Code.

3.3
00:00:32.924 --> 00:00:49.288
Care fills in the Slug from the title and selects Active.

4.1
00:00:49.288 --> 00:00:53.646
Step 4. Add interpretation rules. This step is optional.

4.2
00:00:53.646 --> 00:00:57.094
Care uses these rules to interpret each result.

4.3
00:00:57.094 --> 00:01:03.023
You can add rules to the definition or to its components, but not to both.

5.1
00:01:03.023 --> 00:01:07.892
Step 5. Fill in the additional details. This section is optional.

5.2
00:01:07.892 --> 00:01:11.303
Record the Body Site, the Method that staff use,

5.3
00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:14.574
and the Unit of measure for the result.

6.1
00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:19.197
Step 6. Add components for a test with more than one value.

6.2
00:01:19.197 --> 00:01:24.608
Select Add your first component, then give each component its LOINC code.

6.3
00:01:24.608 --> 00:01:28.739
If the test gives only one value, skip this step.

7.1
00:01:28.739 --> 00:01:33.302
Step 7. Save the observation definition. Select Create.

7.2
00:01:33.302 --> 00:01:38.243
If the slug is already in use, or two ranges of a rule overlap,

7.3
00:01:38.243 --> 00:01:43.291
Care does not save it. Fix them, then select Create again.
